      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{61e30b609e51320b34a45b10|full_name}: Possibly, yes. But on Quest, there's already the issue of players ignoring avatar performance limitations, and just asking everyone to click 'Show avatar'. Which leads to VRChat performing more poorly on Quest.\nI feel like locking more features (such as avatar sounds) behind 'Show avatar' is only going to exacerbate the problem. I'd prefer if players were encourages to create avatars that run well on Quest.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
